        "event": "Heat Advisory",
        "headline": "Heat Advisory issued June 1 at 6:32PM AKDT until June 2 at 8:00PM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Temperatures 80 to 85 expected in areas away from the\ninner channels and outer coast.\n\n* WHERE...City of Hyder, Ketchikan Gateway Borough, and Prince\nof Wales Island.\n\n* WHEN...From 10 AM to 8 PM AKDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Individuals not accustomed to these unusually hot\ntemperatures for this region may experience heat related\nillnesses.",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Expected",
        "sender": "NWS Juneau AK",
        "effective": "2026-06-01T18:32:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-06-02T02:45:00-08:00",
        "areas": "Prince of Wales Island; Ketchikan Gateway Borough; City of Hyder",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Execute",
        "instruction": "Drink plenty of fluids and check up on elderly and vulnerable\nrelatives and neighbors.\n\nYoung children and pets should never be left unattended in\nvehicles under any circumstances as vehicle interiors can reach\nextreme temperatures in as little as 10 minutes\n\nTake extra precautions when working in t",
        "lat": null,
        "lng": null
      },
      {
        "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e4b698a50df2d2fb083a78d5749984cc9e538a5f.001.1",
        "event": "Flood Watch",
        "headline": "Flood Watch issued June 1 at 3:39PM AKDT until June 3 at 10:00AM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Kodiak Island, including the communities of Kodiak City,\nPort Lions, Ouzinkie, Old Harbor.\n\n* WHEN...Through Wednesday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff from heavy rain may result in flooding\nof rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone\nlocations, including Bells Flats. Heavy rain may saturate soils,\nresulting in isolated landslides in areas of steep terrain. Strong\neast to northeast winds",
        "severity": "Severe",
        "certainty": "Possible",
        "urgency": "Future",
        "sender": "NWS Anchorage AK",
        "effective": "2026-06-01T15:39:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-06-03T10:00:00-08:00",
        "areas": "Kodiak Island Northeast; Kodiak Island Southwest",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Prepare",
        "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.\n\nStay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further informat",
        "lat": null,
        "lng": null
      },
      {
